		<item>
		<title>Recent rumor says Roman Reigns had influence in creative direction for top star at SummerSlam</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398015-recent-rumor-says-roman-reigns-had-influence-in-creative-direction-for-top-star-at-summerslam/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398015-recent-rumor-says-roman-reigns-had-influence-in-creative-direction-for-top-star-at-summerslam/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:31:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Oba Femi]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Roman Reigns]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[SummerSlam]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398015</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>According to a column from Conrad Thompson posted to Uncrowned, Roman Reigns is rumored to have had influence&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398015-recent-rumor-says-roman-reigns-had-influence-in-creative-direction-for-top-star-at-summerslam/">Recent rumor says Roman Reigns had influence in creative direction for top star at SummerSlam</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">According to a column from Conrad Thompson posted to <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/wrestling/article/roman-reigns-pushed-for-major-last-minute-change-in-oba-femis-wwe-summerslam-match-this-past-august-234446645.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Uncrowned</a>, Roman Reigns is rumored to have had influence in the creative direction for Oba Femi at Night One of WWE SummerSlam.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thompson says that Reigns strongly advocated for <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/wrestling/live/wwe-summerslam-night-1-results-grades-analysis-oba-femi-conquers-brock-lesnar-in-brutal-torch-passing-punk-retains-orton-returns-060000615.html">Femi&#8217;s Hell in a Cell victory over Brock Lesnar</a> to replace CM Punk&#8217;s WWE Undisputed Championship defense against Cody Rhodes as the main event for Night One. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thompson also writes that the biggest match for WrestleMania 43 is almost going to be Reigns defending the World Heavyweight Championship against Femi, further stating Reigns himself certainly expects that match to happen. Thompson also adds the rumor is that Reigns has been using his voice backstage to keep Femi as strong as possible until the two have their match. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Femi won the King of the Ring at Night of Champions, which made him the top challenger to Reigns for the WWE World Heavyweight Championship at SummerSlam.  However, there were reports stating that WWE changed course in order to build up Femi as a much bigger star, so that when he finally challenges Reigns, the match will have a more big time feel to it. </p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398015-recent-rumor-says-roman-reigns-had-influence-in-creative-direction-for-top-star-at-summerslam/">Recent rumor says Roman Reigns had influence in creative direction for top star at SummerSlam</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398015-recent-rumor-says-roman-reigns-had-influence-in-creative-direction-for-top-star-at-summerslam/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>SPOILERS: Titles change hands at 11-19-26 TNA IMPACT television tapings</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398010-spoilers-titles-change-hands-at-11-19-26-tna-impact-television-tapings/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398010-spoilers-titles-change-hands-at-11-19-26-tna-impact-television-tapings/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:07:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Spoilers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[tapings]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[title changes]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398010</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>PWInsider Elite reports that two titles changed hands at Thursday night TNA tapings at the WinSport Event Centre&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398010-spoilers-titles-change-hands-at-11-19-26-tna-impact-television-tapings/">SPOILERS: Titles change hands at 11-19-26 TNA IMPACT television tapings</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">PWInsider Elite reports that two titles changed hands at Thursday night TNA tapings at the WinSport Event Centre in Calgary, Alberta, Canada.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">AJ Francis defeated Jason Hotch to win the International Title and Elayna Black won the TNA Knockouts Television Championship from M By Elegance. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These matches will air on future episodes of TNA IMPACT on AMC. </p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398010-spoilers-titles-change-hands-at-11-19-26-tna-impact-television-tapings/">SPOILERS: Titles change hands at 11-19-26 TNA IMPACT television tapings</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/398010-spoilers-titles-change-hands-at-11-19-26-tna-impact-television-tapings/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TNA IMPACT on AMC Results &#8211; 11/19/26 (TNA World Title and more!)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/398007-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-19-26-tna-world-title-and-more/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/398007-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-19-26-tna-world-title-and-more/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:43:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/19/26 TNA IMPACT on AMC results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA World Championship]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398007</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Results for this week&#8217;s TNA IMPACT on AMC are courtesy of TNAWrestling.com. TNA Thursday Night iMPACT! on AMC&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/398007-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-19-26-tna-world-title-and-more/">TNA IMPACT on AMC Results &#8211; 11/19/26 (TNA World Title and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Results for this week&#8217;s TNA IMPACT on AMC are courtesy of <a href="https://tnawrestling.com/news/thursday-night-impact-on-amc-results-november-19-2026">TNAWrestling.com</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Thursday Night iMPACT! on AMC is on the air from the WinSport Event Centre in Calgary, AB, Canada. Tonight, KC Navarro and Bear Bronson kick off the night, and in the main event TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth gets his contractual rematch against TNA World Champion Leon Slater.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Bear Bronson vs. KC Navarro &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bear Bronson shoves and slaps Navarro, and Navarro fires back with a slap of his own. Bronson hoists up Navarro, he counters with a DDT, and Dropkicks him. Bronson rolls to the outside, Navarro dives through the ropes, and Bronson catches him. He sets up to send Navarro into the steel steps, Navarro avoids them, and kicks the steps into Bronson’s Knee. He drives down Bronson on the outside with a Hurricanrana off the steel steps.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back inside the ring, Navarro dives into Bear with a Back Elbow Strike, sets up to flip him to the canvas, and Bronson avoids it. He sends Navarro over the ropes, Navarro tries to drop Bronson with a Sunset Flip, and Bronson counters by crushing him. Bronson rains down blows, Chops Navarro, and locks him up against the ropes. He drives down Navarro with a Chokebomb, goes for a cover, and Navarro kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He connects a big right hook onto Navarro, and Navarro fires back with multiple strikes. Navarro cuts down Bronson with a DDT, goes for a cover, and Bronson kicks out at two. Cedric Alexander distracts Navarro, Bronson charges at him, and Navarro rolls him up for a two count. Bronson drives down Navarro with a Blackhole Slam into a cover, and Navarro kicks out at two. Bronson hoists up Navarro for Bear Down, Navarro breaks free, and Bronson shoves him into the ropes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cedric Alexander shoves Navarro towards Bronson to help him out, and trips up Bronson into the ropes instead. Navarro seizes the opportunity to dive into Bear with the 305, into Blessing in Disguise to secure the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>KC Navarro Def. Bear Bronson &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gia Miller is standing by with one half of the TNA World Tag Team Champions Nic Nemeth ahead of his contractual rematch later tonight. He is confident that he will walk out as the TNA World Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cedric Alexander and Bear Bronson are arguing backstage. Eddie Edwards defends Cedric stating he made a mistake, and Bronson storms off with Myers following suit.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Trey Miguel hits the iMPACT! Zone after his TNA World Championship against TNA World Champion Leon Slater at Destination X, and what is next for him. He reflects on his travel issues going into Destination X, he wonders what if, and is confident if they faced off again he would walk away TNA World Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth interrupts him. Nic is confident he is going to be the TNA World Champion by the end of the night, and swears that he will not give Miguel a title shot.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic Nemeth attacks Miguel from behind after Ryan Nemeth distracts him. The Nemeths attack Trey in the ring and Leon Slater rushes to the ring to protect him.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">M by Elegance is with Heather by Elegance after Destination X. M by Elegance chastises Heather stating she has one more chance, and Heather promises the poster reveal will go exactly as it should.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Close out the year with The Biggest Hardy Party ever at the Speaking Rock Casino in El Paso, TX. Admission is free!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Director of Operations Daria Rae is with Brian, and is upset about the FAA travel issues that prevented Hartwell from showing. Brian doesn’t want Daria Rae to be playing favorites, and states that Tasha Steelz and Shayna Baszler will both get their chance at the TNA Knockouts World Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Fire ‘n Flava &amp; TNA Knockouts World Tag Team Champions Apex vs. TNA World Champion Indi Hartwell, Gabby Forza, Allie, &amp; Shotzi Blackheart &#8211; 8-Knockouts Tag Team Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Allie is found down backstage ahead of the match, but the match is continuing. Gabby Forza dives into the ring, flattens Fire ‘n Flava, and the bell rings. Shotzi Blackheart dives through the ropes to wipe out Fire ‘n Flava, and Gabby Forza hoists up Shotzi, sends her flying over the ropes, and she wipes out Apex.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Shotzi rolls Baszler back into the ring, Gabby drives down Baszler, sets up to crush her, and Baszler avoids her. She tags in Serrano, she lands multiple Forearm Shivers onto Gabby, and tags in Hogan. Hogan flips Gabby to the canvas, goes for a cover, and Gabby kicks out at two. Kiera tags in Baszler, who drives a boot into the spine of Forza.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">She locks Forza into an armlock, Forza breaks free, and drives down Shayna. Shayna tags in Steelz, who prevents Forza from getting a tag, and tags in Serrano. She Chops Forza’s collarbone, tags in Kiera, and flips her to the canvas. Gabby tags in Shotzi Blackheart, she German Suplexes Kiera into the turnbuckles, and charges at her in the corner. Kiera avoids her, slams her down, and tags in Steelz.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hogan hipattacks Blackheart in the corner, Steelz locks Shotzi into a Chokehold, and Shotzi breaks free. Tasha Steelz drives a boot into her to slow her up, tags in Baszler, and Baszler tags in Serrano. Baszler drops Shotzi off her knee, and Serrano sets her up for Baszler to drive a knee into Shotzi. Serrano goes for a cover, and Shotzi kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Baszler stomps on Shotzi’s arm, and tags in Hogan. Hogan slams her face-first into the top turnbuckle, tags in Steelz, and Steelz rams into Blackheart in the corner. Blackheart connects a boot to the face of Steelz, knocks Apex and Hogan off the apron, and Steelz answers with a Pumpkick. Steelz goes for a cover, Blackheart kicks out at two, and Hogan prevents a tag by dragging Gabby off the edge of the apron.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Blackheart gets a tag onto Hartwell, she drives down Serrano with a Spinebuster, and Baszler breaks it up. Gabby Forza drives down Baszler with a German Suplex, and Fire ‘n Flava charges at Hartwell and Forza. They catch Fire ‘n Flava, and Hartwell and Forza slam them down with a Fall Away Slam.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Zoey Serrano Supekicks Hartwell, and Shotzi Blackheart soars from the top rope to flatten Apex with a Double Dropkick. Blackheart crushes Steelz in the corner, and Gabby sets her up for Poetry in Motion onto Hogan. Serrano drags Forza out of the ring, and Baszler meets Shotzi in the ring. Serrano rolls back into the ring, Superkicks Shotzi, and Apex sets up for Kill Shot.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Blackheart counters, sends Serrano into Hogan, and Gabby drags Serrano out of the ring. Blackheart takes Steelz to the Upside Down, Baszler locks Shotzi in the Choke Ten Choke, and Serrano German Suplexes Forza into a Kneestrike. She Superkicks Shotzi, rolls her back into the ring, and Hogan drives her down with Face the Music to secure the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Fire ‘n Flava &amp; TNA Knockouts World Tag Team Champions Apex Def. TNA World Champion Indi Hartwell, Gabby Forza, Allie, &amp; Shotzi Blackheart &#8211; 8-Knockouts Tag Team Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA Injury Report presented by CarShield:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Amazing Red is still not clear for in-ring competition due to lingering neck issues from a Danger Zone delivered by Nic Nemeth.</li>



<li>Avery Styles remains out of action due to an ATFL ankle Injury from a recent match.</li>



<li>Frankie Kazarian suffered a head injury from Mustafa Ali at Destination X and remains out of action.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA World Champion Leon Slater is getting warmed up for his upcoming match. Elijah interrupts him, and gives Slater some words of encouragement. The Nemeths interrupt them and attack Slater and Elijah. Director of Authority Santino Marella breaks it up, and Slater is left down holding his neck.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mila Moore, Taryn Terrell, and Harley Hudson make their way into the iMPACT! Zone as the newest generation of The Dollhouse. Terrell shares the story that stems from Sacrifice, and the responsibility they have to nurture the younger talent. She has found her purpose, and sees Harley and Mila as her girls. She will do anything to protect her girls, and has given them a place they belong.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mustafa Ali reflects on the TNA Lockerroom, and how he tried to teach Frankie Kazarian a lesson. He has his eyes on Slater and his upcoming match against Nic Nemeth later tonight.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Rock-Solid Moment of the Night presented by Blue Chew is from KC Navarro’s victory against Bear Bronson tonight.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">John Skyler walks by Elayna and Heather, and Heather states everything is going to work out the way it is supposed to before walking away.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Xia acc. by The Righteous vs. Sofia Sivan &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Xia drives Sivan face first into the top turnbuckle, and slams her head off of it. She lands multiple kicks onto her in the corner, and rams into her. Sivan breaks out of the corner, and drives Double Knees into Xia. She sets up for Michinoku Driver, and Xia escapes. Xia kicks the spine of Sivan, and locks her against the ropes. She drives down Sivan with Darkside and secures the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Xia acc. by The Righteous Def. Sofia Sivan &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the match, Vincent enters the ring with a chair, sits down, and Dutch drags a piece of wood from under the ring. He sets it up under Sivan’s legs, Vincent hands Xia the chair, and she drives it into Sivan.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA International Champion Jason Hotch is joined by Fabian Aichner and announces that in two weeks they’ll go one-on-one for the TNA International Championship. Hotch wants Aichner to bring the same energy he is bringing now. AJ Francis interrupts them, and has his eyes set on the TNA International Championship. Ricky Sosa interrupts Francis.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Director of Authority Santino Marella has a few big announcements. Next week is the TNA Thanksgiving Special, and the week after that TNA Wrestling is bringing back the Triple Threat Revolver Match. Moose and Matt Hardy interrupt him, and Matt needs revenge against syX. Moose wants Matt Hardy to put syX in their rearview mirror for the Triple Threat Revolver. Matt refuses to put syX behind him, and wants Samuel Shaw to pay.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA World Champion Leon Slater vs. TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth &#8211; TNA World Championship</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic Nemeth Headbutts Slater into a Superkick, goes for an early cover, and Slater kicks out at two. He charges at Slater in the corner, drives him down with Neckbreaker into a cover, and Slater kicks out at two. Nemeth follows with a Shot to the Heart into another pin attempt, and Slater kicks out at two once again. Nemeth looks for Danger Zone, Slater avoids it, and sends Nic toppling over the top rope. He soars over the ropes and levels Nic on the outside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater connects two Chops, and Nemeth goes to the eyes of Slater. He Headbutts Slater, sets up to slam him face first into the edge of the apron, and Slater counters. He slams Nic face first into the edge of the apron, and rolls Nic back into the ring. As Slater rolls into the ring, Nic Nemeth sets up for Famouser, and Slater counters with a Powerbomb. Slater goes for a cover, and Nic kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater sets up for a Handspring Back-Elbow, and his neck injury from earlier stops him in his tracks. Nemeth shoves Slater to the outside, and drives him down with a Neckbreaker on the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic rolls back into the ring, Slater follows, and Nemeth discards him to the outside again. Slater rolls back into the ring, Nic sends him to the outside for a third time, and follows after him. He shoves Slater into the steel steps, Slater soars over them, and retaliates with a Superman Forearm Strike.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater sends Nic into the ring, Nemeth drives him down with a Neckbreaker into a cover, and Slater kicks out at two. Nemeth sets up to send Slater into the turnbuckles, Slater reverses it, and sends Nemeth sternum first into the turnbuckles. Nic whips Slater into the turnbuckles, goes for a cover, and Slater kicks out at two. Nemeth locks him in a Chokehold, Slater breaks free with a punch into Jawbreaker, and Dropkicks him. They both go down in the center of the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater rebounds off the ropes with a boot to the face of Nemeth, he climbs to the top rope, and Nic avoids him. He rebounds off the ropes again, and flattens Nic before he climbs to the top turnbuckle. He crushes Nemeth with a Splash, he goes for a cover, and Nic kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater looks for Utopia, and Nic Nemeth prevents it by going for the neck of Slater. Nic drives him down with a Brainbuster, goes for a cover, and Slater kicks out at two. Slater connects a boot to the face of Nemeth off the ropes, Slater climbs to the top rope, and Ryan Nemeth rushes to the ring to distract Slater. Trey Miguel rushes out to the aid of Slater, and chases Ryan up the ramp to the backstage.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic Nemeth connects a Superkick to the mid-section of Slater as he soars off the ropes, he goes for a cover, and Slater kicks out at two. Nemeth stomps Slater&#8217;s leg, sends him face first into the top turnbuckle, and hoists him up onto the ropes. Nic sets up to drive down Slater from the top rope, Slater Headbutts him, and Nic cuts down Slater using the top rope. Nemeth drives down Slater with a Superplex, goes for a cover, and Nic kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nemeth sets up for a Piledriver, and Slater counters by rolling him up. They trade roll up pin attempts until Nic crushes Slater with Famouser, he goes for a cover, and Slater kicks out at two. Nemeth looks for Danger Zone, Slater counters with Utopia, and climbs to the top turnbuckle. He sets up for the Swanton 450, Nemeth rolls out of the way, Nemeth charges at Slater, but crashes into the referee. Slater slams down Nemeth with another Utopia, goes for a cover, but the referee is still down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater checks on the referee, Nemeth seizes the opportunity to Superkick Slater, and goes for a cover. Slater kicks out at two, and the referee topples out of the ring. Nic slides out of the ring, grabs a steel chair from under the ring, and sets up to get back into the ring with it. Elijah attacks Nic from behind with a guitar strap, and rolls Nemeth back into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater seizes the opportunity, connects a big boot to the face of Nemeth, and climbs to the top turnbuckle. He crushes Nemeth with Swanton 450 and secures the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA World Champion Leon Slater Def. TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth &#8211; TNA World Championship</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Thursday Night iMPACT! on AMC goes off the air…</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="Nic Nemeth vs. Leon Slater for the TNA World Title (FULL MATCH) | TNA iMPACT! November 19, 2026" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/voXHjxBtJWI?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/398007-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-19-26-tna-world-title-and-more/">TNA IMPACT on AMC Results &#8211; 11/19/26 (TNA World Title and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/398007-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-19-26-tna-world-title-and-more/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report: &#8216;A-list Hollywood creative team&#8217; involved with movie about former WWE champion</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/398004-report-a-list-hollywood-creative-team-involved-with-movie-about-former-wwe-champion/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/398004-report-a-list-hollywood-creative-team-involved-with-movie-about-former-wwe-champion/#respond</comments>
		
